    "body": "OWNER repair directive: eliminate stale executable routes before production work resumes.\n\nBase: `main@61ceeafa9b289af251fa744caab04127893cf365`.\nCurrent product authority: #251 (`ACTIVE_PHASE = P01`; old A/B/C and tool/executor routes are not product NEXT).\n\nFresh audit found three old communication workflows still capable of routing comment-triggered execution and a separate gh-aw LESTER compiler/source/generated-lock toolchain even though the current R03 production router already says `R03_RETIRED_FROM_AUTOMATION`.\n\nThis candidate:\n- hard-disables the legacy base comment ingress (`if: false`) while preserving an inert compatibility file for older library tests;\n- converts R02B and R02B-v2 to manual-only retirement stubs;\n- removes the old gh-aw LESTER workflow source, generated lock, compiler workflow, and obsolete actionlint exception config;\n- removes workflow-shape tests whose contract required the retired executors to remain live;\n- adds a regression test proving retired routes contain no Windows/self-hosted/Copilot/Task execution and the gh-aw toolchain is absent.\n\nUnderlying parsing/evidence libraries are retained because current security tests still exercise their fail-closed contracts; code presence does not imply activation.\n\nNo physical OWNER-PC runner deregistration is claimed. No production/canon activation.",
